  "body": "What should happen when you redact MSC2716 related events? @erikjohnston does this look sane?\r\n\r\n - \"insertion\" event\r\n    - Undo the steps we take in [`_handle_insertion_event`](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/72935b7c5053af122c8cb5767a3e85a3a0f3a20c/synapse/storage/databases/main/events.py#L1760-L1809)\r\n    - Remove from the `insertion_events` table\r\n    - Remove all of the `insertion_event_edges`\r\n - \"chunk\" event\r\n    - Undo the steps we take in [`_handle_chunk_event`](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/72935b7c5053af122c8cb5767a3e85a3a0f3a20c/synapse/storage/databases/main/events.py#L1811-L1846)\r\n    - Remove from `chunk_events`\r\n - \"marker\" event\r\n    - not merged yet, see https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/pull/10498\r\n    - Undo the steps we take in `_handle_marker_event`\r\n    - We backfill the insertion event in `_handle_marker_event` but I don't think we need to undo that. If they want to redact the insertion event, they can do that separately. We can just redact the \"marker\" event as normal with no special logic.\r\n\r\n---\r\n  \r\nA more general question but what happens when you redact a redaction? Does it cancel the event being redacted?\r\n ",
